    "iconicApps": [
      "fvwm",
      "xterm",
      "xcalc",
      "xclock"
    ],
    "blurb": "OpenBSD 7.9, May 2026: the security-first BSD that gave the world OpenSSH, pf and LibreSSL, still shipping fvwm 2.2 as the default window manager in its own X tree, Xenocara — here on amd64 with the classic X applications one click away.",
    "notes": "Live streamhost station. Cold boot autologs root on ttyC0 and starts X (vesa, 1024x768) with an xterm, xclock, xeyes and xcalc under fvwm; left- or right-click the desktop for the applications menu, middle-click for the window list. usb-tablet absolute pointer via an xf86-input-ws calibration InputClass. disk.qcow2 is the single block device and carries the golden vmstate. One vCPU on purpose: with two, the guest loses keyboard interrupts under X."
  },
